      "Why is splitting one CRUD entity into one microservice often a poor boundary rule?",
      "A service should own a cohesive business capability and its invariants, not merely a database table. Table-based splitting can force chatty network calls and distributed transactions for ordinary business operations. Identify bounded contexts, ownership, change frequency, and independent deployment needs. A modular monolith can preserve those boundaries until separate deployment solves an actual operational problem.",
