      "Database ownership",
      "Can services share one database server while still owning separate data?",
      "Physical infrastructure can be shared, but ownership requires private schemas or stores, access controls, and contracts that prevent one service from directly changing another's tables. Cross-service joins and shared migration dependencies erode independent evolution. Choose physical isolation when workload, security, or availability requires it; database-per-service describes ownership, not a mandatory dedicated machine per service.",
