      "Outer joins and filter placement",
      "Why can filtering a right-side column in WHERE remove rows from a LEFT JOIN?",
      "A left join preserves unmatched left rows by supplying NULLs for the right side. A WHERE predicate requiring a matching right-side value usually rejects those rows, making that result behave like an inner join. Put a right-side qualification in ON when unmatched left rows must remain. Choose placement according to the intended result, not a blanket performance rule.",
