      "Capacity reasoning",
      "How would you turn a daily request count into an initial capacity estimate?",
      "Convert daily volume into average requests per second, then model peak factors, read/write mix, payload size, concurrency, and latency objectives. Averages alone miss bursts and long-running work. State assumptions openly, estimate the bottleneck, and validate with load testing. Capacity planning should include failure headroom rather than assigning every replica full steady-state utilization.",
