      "What race should you consider when invalidating a cache after a database write?",
      "A concurrent reader may load an old value and repopulate the cache around the write/invalidation sequence. Choose a strategy matching tolerated staleness, such as bounded TTLs, versioned values, or coordinated update handling. Cache-aside improves access cost but does not itself provide strong consistency. Keep the authoritative invariant in a suitable durable store.",
