      "If all that customer's work maps to one partition key, additional partitions do not distribute the hot key. Consider a key with appropriate distribution, workload isolation, bounded fan-out, or sharded subkeys where ordering and transaction requirements permit them. More shards add routing and aggregation complexity. Measure whether the bottleneck is a key, a query, or a shared dependency first.",
